{
  "work_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii",
  "source_path": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii.json",
  "source_language": "chu",
  "target_language": "eng",
  "provenance": {
    "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29": {
      "model": "gpt-6.1-sol",
      "prompt_version": "bulk-2026-10-12",
      "date": "2026-10-29",
      "script": "__main__"
    }
  },
  "translations": [
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.88v.s1",
      "source_sha256": "af6147a6e8625b7b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "March 20. The martyrdom of Saints Terentius, Africanus, and Pompeius. While Decius was reigning"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.88v.s2",
      "source_sha256": "52242daedbb376ae",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "over the Roman dominion and wishing to draw everyone to his own faith—for he had the devil as his father—"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.88v.s3",
      "source_sha256": "24b1c49adeb91e10",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "he sent orders throughout his empire that all who called upon the name of Christ"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.88v.s4",
      "source_sha256": "bf9d14b622de22a2",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "should be induced to eat defiled food. If any resisted this, they were to be handed over for judgment."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.88v.s5",
      "source_sha256": "06ec9a45fca64b6b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He also sent this impious command to Africa, to Fortunatianus, the governor of Africa."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.88v.s6",
      "source_sha256": "eb0827333bdeeff5",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When the emperor's command reached his jurisdiction, the governor received the emperor's letter and sat on the judgment seat."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.88v.s7",
      "source_sha256": "02fbb70f07a05fac",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He ordered the townspeople to be seized and brought in, and instruments of torture to be laid before them."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38r.s1",
      "source_sha256": "e6dda15ea6f65fbf",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He said to them: “Sacrifice to the gods. Otherwise, you will die a terrible death.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38r.s2",
      "source_sha256": "bf0ba2e8646a8da5",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Many of the people, seeing the instruments of torture and fearing the threats, obeyed the governor"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38r.s3",
      "source_sha256": "5d55e128f9d7b8e6",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and abandoned the faith of Christ. But some of them, forty in number, pledged"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38r.s4",
      "source_sha256": "b2c747b07bfd461f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "to meet their end [?], gathering together. And they said with confidence to one another: “Take care, brothers."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38r.s5",
      "source_sha256": "81fbaddb76bbd4f7",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Let us not deny our Lord Jesus Christ, so that he in turn will not deny us."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38r.s6",
      "source_sha256": "9c100ed4de12c8da",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Understand that the Lord has already said: ‘Do not fear those who kill the body"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38r.s7",
      "source_sha256": "f633aea7605e2f21",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "but cannot kill the soul. Rather, fear the one who can"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38r.s8",
      "source_sha256": "cb4829c42a5dacfe",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "destroy both soul and body in the fiery [?].’” They strengthened one another with these words."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38r.s9",
      "source_sha256": "436684ffb507918b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Fortunatianus the governor said: “I see that you are men of fine stature, handsome and wise in speech."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38r.s10",
      "source_sha256": "3c073ff79407a98e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "How have you given yourselves over to such deception, deception, confessing one God and a certain Christ,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38r.s11",
      "source_sha256": "a7af5727a600b7f9",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "whom Jewish youths crucified as a criminal?” The holy martyr Terentius, speaking for them all, said:"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38v.s1",
      "source_sha256": "7a1c127935b4a1d0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "“If the governor knew the power of the crucified one, he would abandon the vain deception of idols"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38v.s2",
      "source_sha256": "51704871865d0300",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and worship him and please him, the true Son, the benefactor from the Father,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38v.s3",
      "source_sha256": "e523771f789c5c30",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "compassionate and merciful, who at the Father's bidding and command came down to earth"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38v.s4",
      "source_sha256": "cc9ef300cd617dab",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and adorned his divinity with human nature, and who also endured the cross for our salvation.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38v.s5",
      "source_sha256": "c518f1c4613dd3d8",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When Fortunatianus the governor heard this, he said to the saints: “Will you sacrifice, or shall I lay hands on your limbs and destroy you?” Terentius said:"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38v.s6",
      "source_sha256": "7c04a25bf2d04b40",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "“Did you think we would be frightened by threats? We are not so weak that we would abandon the giver of life"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38v.s7",
      "source_sha256": "c65b744dcb768009",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and worship foreign gods. Just do whatever you wish to us.” Then the governor became angry."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38v.s8",
      "source_sha256": "502a1879b48b1450",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He ordered their clothes to be torn off and the prisoners to be led into the temple of the idols. These shrines were gilded and adorned"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38v.s9",
      "source_sha256": "7ec006f350eb3bc0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "with costly splendor. The governor entered and said to them, “Offer sacrifice to the great-minded god Heracles."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.38v.s10",
      "source_sha256": "8bf0170fbd945f15",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "You see his glory and his power.” Terentius said, “You are deceiving yourself, not knowing what is good for you."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89r.s1",
      "source_sha256": "0dc79e37dd43d8b0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "For these whom you regard as gods are stone, wood, bronze, and iron, adorned with gold to lead people astray"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89r.s2",
      "source_sha256": "f9689622cc2ab1d7",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "from eternal life. For they neither see nor speak nor walk nor hear, being stones,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89r.s3",
      "source_sha256": "ea3cb0afe7bab866",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "carved by human beings and fashioned in human form. So speak to your gods,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89r.s4",
      "source_sha256": "6a83c01a7549a8b0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "as you consider them, and see whether they can help themselves or inflict [?] on anyone who is angry with them.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89r.s5",
      "source_sha256": "9af38929b0850c5e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Hearing this, the governor became furious and ordered Terentius and Africanus,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89r.s6",
      "source_sha256": "f418e779e574b6dc",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Maximus and Pompeius, to be thrown into the inner prison"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89r.s7",
      "source_sha256": "eed378476a38e6d2",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and kept under the strictest guard, saying, “I will question them on [?] day.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89r.s8",
      "source_sha256": "ec9b7696e6865e54",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "But blessed Zeno, Alexander, and Theodore, together with their companions, forty-six in number,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89r.s9",
      "source_sha256": "91ae0e93943a1c57",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "he ordered to be brought before the judgment seat. He said to them, “You have gained nothing by your earlier argument."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89r.s10",
      "source_sha256": "47de83ff4215d041",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Listen to me and offer sacrifice to great-minded Heracles.” They answered,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89r.s11",
      "source_sha256": "0cbc3eb7e3feb4bf",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "“We have told you many times, including at your first interrogation, that we are Christians,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89r.s12",
      "source_sha256": "e2d625984da69194",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and you will not persuade us to worship at unclean shrines. For we are ready, when you question us,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89v.s1",
      "source_sha256": "445a388efee1cfd5",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "to answer.” The governor said, “Will you not listen to me when I appeal to you?"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89v.s2",
      "source_sha256": "178da01f35751c7f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Then you are forcing me to carry out the emperor’s command and inflict further things on you.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89v.s3",
      "source_sha256": "490c5e527a64b62f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He ordered them to be beaten with knotted rods and ox sinews. The holy martyrs stretched out their hands toward heaven"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89v.s4",
      "source_sha256": "1c81e966c1e328c3",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and cried out in a loud voice, “Look upon us, O God, and help your servants, and deliver us from the adversary!”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89v.s5",
      "source_sha256": "3ccb06946a1dea56",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Hearing this, the governor ordered them to be beaten still more severely, until thirty centurions had taken turns beating each of them."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89v.s6",
      "source_sha256": "47155e30176ec2e1",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "As the saints were being beaten, the [?] and the rods wore out."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89v.s7",
      "source_sha256": "b898b8d53da17a92",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Then, in a fury, he ordered them to be beaten with knotty pieces of wood, so that even their internal organs could now be seen."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89v.s8",
      "source_sha256": "d0ede7d809a31f08",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "This was what the saints looked like, so that everyone marveled at their endurance."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89v.s9",
      "source_sha256": "9e6973973f9be3b3",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "After they had been tortured severely, the governor said, “At least offer sacrifice now, you wretches, and I will release you.” But the saints remained silent,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89v.s10",
      "source_sha256": "da51c3647f112f68",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "giving him no answer. Again the governor ordered nails to be heated and their backs burned with them."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.89v.s11",
      "source_sha256": "c76fc4291fab415d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "And when they were torturing them severely, he ordered strong vinegar mixed with salt"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s1",
      "source_sha256": "c8337fa160c8d6e2",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "to be poured onto their backs, and their wounds to be rubbed with coarse cloth."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s2",
      "source_sha256": "73128a9862658cb4",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The saints looked up to heaven: “Lord God, who delivered"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s3",
      "source_sha256": "f91746808ceb026e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "your three holy youths, Hananiah, Azariah, and Mishael, from the fiery furnace"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s4",
      "source_sha256": "a1daa629339952cd",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and did not allow them to suffer harm; who delivered Daniel from the lions’ mouths"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s5",
      "source_sha256": "b206bbafdb0b21dc",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and preserved Moses from Pharaoh’s hand;"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s6",
      "source_sha256": "8fdb6df0c76bed59",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who saved Thecla from the fire, from the arena, and from the beasts; who work"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s7",
      "source_sha256": "d869f2340885ae89",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and bestow banners on those you love; who raised up the shepherd of the sheep, our Lord Jesus Christ;"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s8",
      "source_sha256": "d3e701c25c721e87",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "who have bestowed many and varied blessings; who have made light shine and have driven darkness"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s9",
      "source_sha256": "a79a37d02b0c7335",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "away; who roll up heaven like a hide; who count the stars of heaven"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s10",
      "source_sha256": "8239cb0b518bbe9f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and the sand of the sea, and have adorned truth: hear us as we pray to you, O Christ,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s11",
      "source_sha256": "5a7781e40887fafc",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and help us, for yours are the glory and the power forever. Amen.” When the saints had finished their prayer"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s12",
      "source_sha256": "91b887c66ad8352c",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and said “Amen,” the governor again ordered them to be hung up and their sides scraped. As the saints were being flayed for many hours,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90r.s13",
      "source_sha256": "2432962c06f29c54",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "a stream of blood flowed from their holy bodies, so that the great quantity of blood"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s1",
      "source_sha256": "f9049f10f891b31d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "soaked the attendants’ clothes. Yet they paid no heed to the tortures, for Christ was giving them relief"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s2",
      "source_sha256": "d24b770a26f6f110",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and helping them. The governor said to them, “Have the tortures persuaded you"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s3",
      "source_sha256": "5dffb2ce415b0899",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "to give up the madness you possess, you who are doomed to a miserable death,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s4",
      "source_sha256": "534a3e49a91db92f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "or do you persist in your false belief?” But the saints gave him no answer."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s5",
      "source_sha256": "e596afb5cedfeadb",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Instead, they looked up to heaven and said, “You who demolished the city of Sodom with fire and laid it waste,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s6",
      "source_sha256": "15577709f38000ff",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "send your help now as well, and destroy this godless madness"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s7",
      "source_sha256": "1486f5d4670f26b4",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and overthrow their idols.” Then, making the sign of the cross on their faces,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s8",
      "source_sha256": "48e4f3a65b863394",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "they blew upon the idols, and immediately they crumbled and became like dust."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s9",
      "source_sha256": "117b31b82dd1b387",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The saints said to the lawless governor, “Look at the things you worship!"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s10",
      "source_sha256": "fb26af8c14e73ebf",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Where is their empty strength? Were they able to help themselves?” While the saints were saying this,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s11",
      "source_sha256": "d98ef40c82888987",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "the temple of the idols also collapsed. The governor became enraged at the destruction of his gods."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s12",
      "source_sha256": "80e96df77d24d3fe",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He ordered the saints to be put to death by the sword. When the saints received the sentence, they went away rejoicing and praising the Lord."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.90v.s13",
      "source_sha256": "0d40fe7c1a81c0d7",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When they reached the appointed place, they knelt down and stretched out"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91r.s1",
      "source_sha256": "a96a48e2f171d6a5",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "their necks, and died by the sword, confessing Christ."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91r.s2",
      "source_sha256": "4455492b3ea22c7d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Christians came, took their bodies, and laid them in a place of honor."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91r.s3",
      "source_sha256": "e3b57832d2338e31",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "After these saints had died, the lawless governor ordered Terentius and Africanus to be brought in."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91r.s4",
      "source_sha256": "a3e97ab74f61a3a6",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He said to them, “Offer sacrifices to the gods. Otherwise, I will put you both to a cruel death,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91r.s5",
      "source_sha256": "cd04200c8d74569d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and there is no god who will deliver you from my hands.” The two saints replied, “We have told you many times"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91r.s6",
      "source_sha256": "711a182272b01b4b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "that we are Christians and place our hope in Christ."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91r.s7",
      "source_sha256": "06e8720cc91f2bf6",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "We will not bow down to unclean demons or serve your gods, and we care nothing for your tortures."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91r.s8",
      "source_sha256": "94ba88f6b5964bb7",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "So devise as many tortures against us as you wish. For we trust in God that you will be defeated by us, his servants,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91r.s9",
      "source_sha256": "40cb0bc67fa81eae",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "just as your father the devil was defeated.” When the governor heard this, he ordered them to be thrown into prison"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91r.s10",
      "source_sha256": "df6a49c30dd54043",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and chains to be placed around their necks, on their hands, and on their feet, and for them to be kept under guard in this condition."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91r.s11",
      "source_sha256": "a5a045d030144bab",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The servants did as they had been commanded. He also ordered iron tridents to be laid beneath them,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91r.s12",
      "source_sha256": "3d9b7fdc366602cb",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and that no Christian should be allowed to visit them or give them food."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91v.s1",
      "source_sha256": "e0eb1795b4e8bb63",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "At midnight, while the two saints were praying, a great light shone around them in the prison."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91v.s2",
      "source_sha256": "e566d9de72e98489",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "An angel of the Lord stood before them and said, “Rise and rest.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91v.s3",
      "source_sha256": "f3e8db36bb7bdd9e",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The angel approached and touched the chains that lay around their necks,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91v.s4",
      "source_sha256": "b61862bd736bd782",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and immediately the chains fell from their bodies."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91v.s5",
      "source_sha256": "8bc2853be23234ac",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Before them stood a table prepared with all kinds of good food."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91v.s6",
      "source_sha256": "cd4eeda467835ac0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The angel said to them, “Take some of the food set before you,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91v.s7",
      "source_sha256": "73799f1d459854a9",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "which the Lord God has sent you.” The two saints blessed the Lord and then ate the food."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91v.s8",
      "source_sha256": "d748c9fd7f42e33b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When the prison guards saw the light, they rushed inside to see the light more clearly."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91v.s9",
      "source_sha256": "5f80fc37c85914fc",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When they entered, they found the two saints rejoicing, and they went out in fear."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91v.s10",
      "source_sha256": "13767e8ab34b4238",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "They reported to the governor what they had seen. On the third day, he ordered the saints to be brought before the judgment seat."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91v.s11",
      "source_sha256": "b405df72b37909fd",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When the two saints stood before the governor, he said to them, “Have the tortures taught you your lesson, then?”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.91v.s12",
      "source_sha256": "ba30dbb2d5c176b8",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "“O you wicked, demon-possessed ones! Repent and sacrifice to the gods.” Saint Terence said, “This torture, for me"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92r.s1",
      "source_sha256": "e4eb34b4ee684f86",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and for those who love Christ, may it be! For the foolishness of God is wiser than human beings. For human wisdom"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92r.s2",
      "source_sha256": "0bdce58425fee484",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "is foolishness before God. I would be senseless and raving, like you,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92r.s3",
      "source_sha256": "c1d3cc08fdefbfc8",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "if I abandoned God and worshiped demons.” The governor became angry and ordered them to be flayed. As the two saints were being scraped, they prayed, saying, “Jesus Christ,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92r.s4",
      "source_sha256": "97c3a9f2e5f44560",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "Son of the living God, light of Christians who abides forever, indestructible faith,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92r.s5",
      "source_sha256": "516b7aacbfca7bbb",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "appear and help us both, and do not put us to shame before your face.”"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92r.s6",
      "source_sha256": "2ebe192b7f9d2847",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "While the servants were flaying them and Christ was easing their torments, the two saints felt no pain."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92r.s7",
      "source_sha256": "0d394e93261fd93d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The governor became angry and ordered them to be taken down from the wooden frame and led into prison."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92r.s8",
      "source_sha256": "3066e7f2e15adfbf",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "He summoned all the beast-charmers and ordered them to bring as many creatures as they had,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92r.s9",
      "source_sha256": "d2448b91ed3afe88",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "fierce and vicious ones—asps, vipers, and horned snakes—and to throw them in and shut them up with the two saints."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92r.s10",
      "source_sha256": "388c1b50396ccc96",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The creatures crawled about before their feet as they sat,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92r.s11",
      "source_sha256": "41ac5d1b3a8faf62",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and did not touch them at all. The two saints sang and praised God."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92r.s12",
      "source_sha256": "f37c00fa7734b8e8",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The creatures remained shut up with them for three days and three nights. On the fourth day, the governor sent men at night"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92v.s1",
      "source_sha256": "ac949506e0d07df4",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "to see whether the two saints had been killed by the creatures. Those who had been sent came to the prison doors to listen."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92v.s2",
      "source_sha256": "c7948c352708cd2b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "They heard them singing and praising God. Wishing to see more clearly,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92v.s3",
      "source_sha256": "abc06c028750f738",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "they climbed onto the prison building and looked down through the small doors."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92v.s4",
      "source_sha256": "223e3b7af6e0b3d2",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "They saw the two saints sitting and an angel of the Lord standing before the creatures,"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92v.s5",
      "source_sha256": "54c8dfef387b0b85",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "not allowing them to come near. They ran and reported to the governor what they had seen."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92v.s6",
      "source_sha256": "a5d5bd3c861b49b4",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The governor rose early in the morning, sat on the judgment seat, and ordered the charmers to take the creatures away"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92v.s7",
      "source_sha256": "ed22df5496c86d9d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and to bring the two saints before the judgment seat. The charmers went and, wishing to approach the doors"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92v.s8",
      "source_sha256": "e95b15f13cdadd57",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "so that the creatures would come to them, called them with their spells, but the creatures did not obey them."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92v.s9",
      "source_sha256": "a0fcf8271b0835ae",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When they opened the prison doors, all the creatures came out together"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92v.s10",
      "source_sha256": "ffa92d575dd9f47a",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "and killed all the people they found standing there. Then they went away into deserted places."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92v.s11",
      "source_sha256": "559f2a6c550b83b3",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "The prison guards went, took the two saints, and led them to the governor."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.92v.s12",
      "source_sha256": "fce0e58653b69ed3",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 25,
      "text": "When the tormentor saw that the two saints had suffered no harm at all, he flew into a rage"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.93r.s1",
      "source_sha256": "fc96cbe1139f08ab",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 8,
      "text": "He gave his verdict concerning them: to put them to death with the sword. The two saints went away rejoicing, singing and saying:"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.93r.s2",
      "source_sha256": "db7e93b5bdec200f",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 8,
      "text": "“He saved us from those who afflicted us and prevailed over those who hated us.” The soldiers appointed to this task"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.93r.s3",
      "source_sha256": "8cc1b738aa35e30b",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 8,
      "text": "took up the sword and cut off the heads of the two saints. And they died confessing Christ."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.93r.s4",
      "source_sha256": "1270b5afd6a2412d",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 8,
      "text": "Christian men came and took the bodies of the two saints, carefully prepared them for burial, and laid them in a place"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.93r.s5",
      "source_sha256": "559bec991c116570",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 8,
      "text": "of honor, two miles away from the city of Rome. The saints suffered martyrdom—"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.93r.s6",
      "source_sha256": "e7bb6fd8e0e7d142",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 8,
      "text": "Terentius and Africanus, Maximus and Pompey, and their companions—under the emperor and persecutor Decius"
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.93r.s7",
      "source_sha256": "6e16cec35d4f3745",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 8,
      "text": "and Valerian, while our Lord Jesus Christ reigns over us."
    },
    {
      "chunk_id": "ccmh-supr/passio-terentii#Supr.93r.s8",
      "source_sha256": "49b5c03be17c35a0",
      "provenance": "gpt-6.1-sol/bulk-2026-10-12/2026-10-29",
      "group_size": 8,
      "text": "To him be glory and dominion forever and ever. Amen."
    }
  ]
}
